{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339337-rituals-and-their-usage","id":1339337,"title":"Rituals and their usage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-04T05:19:36-07:00","id":1339337,"title":"Rituals and their usage","content":"Hi All,<br /> <br /> I've recently started leading a MtA game to a group of friends.<br /> However, since it's been a while since I've last played it, it seems hat I have either forgotten some things or I was a complete idiot when I was playing it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But, from what I can see and what my players (namely, one of them, the one that tends to break games) showed me, it looks like, if you have Life 3 and an odd other sphere, you can basically make yourself a beast.<br /> <br /> I mean, using rituals it seems they could (inside 10 days or so) basically make themselves have all attributes at 5, ability to soak lethal/agg damage, have a mind shield and several other things for the next 6 months. And since they cast the ritual in a sanctum and have a unique instrument, they basically have a difficulty of 3, which makes it trivial to achieve the successes needed.<br /> <br /> Am I really missing something or is it really possible to perform a multitude of rituals over 2 weeks and basically trample over stuff for the next 6 months? I mean, I could resort to moving the sanctum or the unique instrument out of the picture, but I would rather have other options.<br /> <br /> So, any input or help is appreciated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25677-danzaburo","name":"Danzaburo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T06:23:35-07:00","id":1339347,"title":"","content":"With rituals/Extended rolls, it's indeed possible to get some very potent effects going. And all the things listed are pretty much a staple of basic Mage offense/defense, if they are indeed inclined to go into the thick of it; The mind shiuld though, that's pretty much a thing that most have going, if they know what's out there.<br /> <br /> Now, regarding the possibility of making it all last six months...yes, also doable. Given that they are all spells that the mage in question does not need to focus on constantly, they can pretty much all be in effect.<br /> <br /> Howeverrr....if we go into the topic of raised physical stats, there are some safeguards in place, so to speak; If the Mage pushes stats above their human limits, or otherwise changes form 'purely human', they introduce Pattern Bleeding (i.e. 1 unsoakable lethal damage per day, unless feeding on quintessence daily) and permanent paradox. The pattern bleeding only goes away if the changes are made *permanent*, and pushing outside of the human range can also introduce physical or genetic flaws as per Storyteller call.<br /> <br /> But, essentially, to answer your original question? Yes, yes that's all doable. But - and it's a big but - that Mage also radiates 'I AM ZE MAGIC' to everything and everyone that can detect such things. The more a Mage has running effects going, the more they become a beacon for anything that might be interested in things like that - good and bad - and last but not least, the Technocracy; Walking around with a bucket of effects running is like shouting to them &quot;Hey, I'm a Tradition Mage!&quot;. And the moment the Technocracy finds that out, they are going to start to monitor, dig into the character's background, watch his financial transactions, check out the extended family, etc. etc.<br /> <br /> Of course this is just what might happen if the whole Ritual shebang actually succeeds. Remember that rituals, especially those with a lot of built up successes, also can end disastrously if Paradox (i.e. botches) strike. Sure, Willpower and Quintessence can stave things off, but it's still a risk. The best way, by the way, to limit such things is to keep the amount of Quintessence available to characters low - Quint is the easiest way to lower Arete difficulties, and handling anything aggravated.<br /> <br /> Last but not least, hubris is a big theme in mage - hubris and subtlety. If the character's hubris grows so much that he thinks he can walk around all pimped up and radiant, it's a simple thing to also suffer the consequences if they dare to piss off the wrong people. See the aformentioned Technocracy agents. Or heck, if the Mage getting into a pissing match with an (unknownst to them) Werewolf might make that character realize sooner than later, that there are things out there that have headbutting contests with agg-soaking, high-stat characters for fun and rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T07:03:52-07:00","id":1339365,"title":"","content":"Also, depending on whether you count an Effect having an extended duration as being an &quot;active Effect&quot;, you start to run up against the Domino Effect. Every two concurrent Effects the mage has running increases the difficulty of subsequent Arete rolls by +1. Some like to say that it doesn't count unless the Effect requires active maintenance (&quot;concentration&quot;), but otherwise every plate the mage has spinning makes starting up additional plates harder. This is why mages tend to be selective about what Effects they have running, because it could complicate matters if they need to weave new Effects on the fly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Additionally, a mage's magick has a consequence above and beyond what Ambrosia and I mentioned. Namely Resonance (and Synergy). If you've got ANY Effect running continuously for six months, I as Storyteller would use that as license to start giving the character dots of Resonance/Synergy to match the &quot;flavor&quot; of the Effect. Making the mage even more likely to stand out, as even Sleepers begin to notice the uncanny air surrounding the mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 10-04-2019, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T07:20:39-07:00","id":1339370,"title":"","content":"Yeah, thing is the listed effects so far aren't counting as concentration-requiring effects. They're pretty much passives.<br /> Though that resonance idea, I like. It very much fits the idea of Resonance, and gives another angle where it might actually matter. It could be a form of Temporary Resonance that builds up over time, but equally also takes time to leave the mage again, taking the same amount of time to dissipate. I also have a feeling (though I can't point at a specific one) that is very trope-y.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T13:26:14-07:00","id":1339431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339337-rituals-and-their-usage?p=1339347#post1339347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With rituals/Extended rolls, it's indeed possible to get some very potent effects going. And all the things listed are pretty much a staple of basic Mage offense/defense, if they are indeed inclined to go into the thick of it; The mind shiuld though, that's pretty much a thing that most have going, if they know what's out there.<br /> <br /> Now, regarding the possibility of making it all last six months...yes, also doable. Given that they are all spells that the mage in question does not need to focus on constantly, they can pretty much all be in effect.<br /> <br /> Howeverrr....if we go into the topic of raised physical stats, there are some safeguards in place, so to speak; If the Mage pushes stats above their human limits, or otherwise changes form 'purely human', they introduce Pattern Bleeding (i.e. 1 unsoakable lethal damage per day, unless feeding on quintessence daily) and permanent paradox. The pattern bleeding only goes away if the changes are made *permanent*, and pushing outside of the human range can also introduce physical or genetic flaws as per Storyteller call.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, they don't go over the human limit, 5 in all is max, so no pattern bleeding then.<br /> Problem is that I have a hard time differentiating between spells that can and can't be cast as ritual. Ok, there are obvious ones like &quot;fireball&quot; and stuff, but everything that can be used as a buff can be case for the next 6 months.. which makes my life extremely hard as it narrows my playing/planning field.. Ok, having stuff at 5 and various buffs in some situations isn't much, but still..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, essentially, to answer your original question? Yes, yes that's all doable. But - and it's a big but - that Mage also radiates 'I AM ZE MAGIC' to everything and everyone that can detect such things. The more a Mage has running effects going, the more they become a beacon for anything that might be interested in things like that - good and bad - and last but not least, the Technocracy; Walking around with a bucket of effects running is like shouting to them &quot;Hey, I'm a Tradition Mage!&quot;. And the moment the Technocracy finds that out, they are going to start to monitor, dig into the character's background, watch his financial transactions, check out the extended family, etc. etc. </div> </div> </div>Hmm.. I never got the feeling that having so many effects can be detrimental. Is there anywhere I can see this in more details? better yet, how it affects him gamewise? I mean, if I'm going with the &quot;you attract trouble like flame moths&quot; I'm guessing I will needs some hard data.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Otherwise it will be just GM giving the offending player a hard time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course this is just what might happen if the whole Ritual shebang actually succeeds. Remember that rituals, especially those with a lot of built up successes, also can end disastrously if Paradox (i.e. botches) strike. Sure, Willpower and Quintessence can stave things off, but it's still a risk. The best way, by the way, to limit such things is to keep the amount of Quintessence available to characters low - Quint is the easiest way to lower Arete difficulties, and handling anything aggravated. </div> </div> </div>well, that was my hope.. however, the player in question (powerplayer, to be more precise) has all the neat little things like his own sanctum, node, cult, etc.. which basically has him throwing 5 dices with diff 3, having a really small chance to fail... Of course, once I got wind of his plans and how he plans to use the above assets, I could actually go and say &quot;well, you can't have those&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Last but not least, hubris is a big theme in mage - hubris and subtlety. If the character's hubris grows so much that he thinks he can walk around all pimped up and radiant, it's a simple thing to also suffer the consequences if they dare to piss off the wrong people. See the aformentioned Technocracy agents. Or heck, if the Mage getting into a pissing match with an (unknownst to them) Werewolf might make that character realize sooner than later, that there are things out there that have headbutting contests with agg-soaking, high-stat characters for fun and rank. </div> </div> </div>yup.. I was thinking about that as well.. problem is that the other players are not so powerplayerishly oriented and have normal chars. Which means that anything I throw at them (be it supernatural or Technocracy) will probably destroy the others. Especially since he has (of course) Arcana at 5<br /> <br /> As for Resonance, I must admit I haven't dived into it so I don't know actually how to incorporate that or even how it would make any difference. I will need to look into it and see.<br /> <br /> In the end, I really do not want to go and say to him: &quot;ok, let's trim this down a bit&quot; as it would be:<br /> a) gimping his style (in his eyes)<br /> ) making me look like a bad GM since he had to tone down on his char and make adjustments for me<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25677-danzaburo","name":"Danzaburo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T13:44:43-07:00","id":1339437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Danzaburo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339337-rituals-and-their-usage?p=1339431#post1339431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.. I never got the feeling that having so many effects can be detrimental. Is there anywhere I can see this in more details? better yet, how it affects him gamewise? I mean, if I'm going with the &quot;you attract trouble like flame moths&quot; I'm guessing I will needs some hard data.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Otherwise it will be just GM giving the offending player a hard time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Prime 1 can detect magic and it's relative potency. Prime 1/Corr 3 can do so in very large areas. Technocrats have radars to detect this sort of stuff. They don't have enough manpower to go after each and every &quot;dot&quot; of magic that appears in the radar (it detects everything supernatural and there's a lot of supernatural in any given city, it seems) but they do look big enough powersources for control, or (if dangerous) erradication.<br /> <br /> Some other beings also can detect this.<br /> <br /> It doesn't need to be detrimental ALL the time. It's said that mages sometimes carry tass arround to look powerful to other mages (you don't want to mess with this much magick bro!). Having a super sparkly aura marks you as &quot;dangerously magical&quot; to vampires that use Auspex, but this also means they may decide to talk with you rather than try to eat you (albeit some could argue that's just as dangerous, if not more).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-04-2019, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T14:50:19-07:00","id":1339447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Resonance, I must admit I haven't dived into it so I don't know actually how to incorporate that or even how it would make any difference. I will need to look into it and see. </div> </div> </div>You should. As with the &quot;too much magick aura&quot; it's mostly something that marks you as weird, altrough it can have more impactful and evident effects if it's very strong. As per M20 this is talked on Book of Secrets and the core<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> yup.. I was thinking about that as well.. problem is that the other players are not so powerplayerishly oriented and have normal chars. Which means that anything I throw at them (be it supernatural or Technocracy) will probably destroy the others. Especially since he has (of course) Arcana at 5 </div> </div> </div>Ah, the <i>classic </i>problem.<br /> <br /> So, your player has discovered the sweet, sweet, nectar of &quot;Ritual abuse&quot;. What to do?.<br /> <br /> Well, there's several things that were already mentioned in the thread, I will add a few:<br /> *A lot of magick makes a lot of noise that will be heard. This ain't always *bad*, but make it known that actions have consequences in the world. Even magical actions (especially magical actions). Not even Arcane 5 it's going to hide you forever.<br /> *A lot of magick generates a lot of Resonance. Seek it up, it's a very important and complex rule, if very disregarded. This and Paradox are the representation of &quot;if you change the world with magick, the world will change you back&quot;<br /> *Risk it's to be rewarded, rituals aren't free. The player it's taking a lot of (calculated) risk,<i> it's ok if he reaps great power. </i>That being said, he still needs to roll each 6 months. Dice are the friends of the Storyteller and the enemy of the players in all RPG: Given time he WILL botch, no matter the amount of Quint, WP and Sanctums used.<br /> *Don't allow downtime w/o explanation. Characters are people that need to eat, crap, sleep, get money...and most likely can't be up all the time casting rituals<br /> *No free Quint. If players wasted all their Node in the story, chances are that the downtime it's going to see them expending Quint too.<br /> *Cults are people too, they aren't ritual bateries you can abuse. They expect stuff from the Mage and the rituals, if they don't get it they leave. They can also be targeted by enemies if it's evident they're empowering the mage<br /> <br /> All that being said, Rituals are intended to be the most powerful tool of mages. And it shows, if you can capitalize them.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> But make no mistake, as poorly balanced as Mage undoubtedly is, what you're depicting isn't a rules problem but a social problem that happens when different players have different expectations about the game they're playing.<br /> <br /> This it's not something that can be solved with any amount of ruling (nor RAW nor Homemade). Much more &quot;balanced games&quot; can have this problem (I know D&amp;D players <i>have</i> this problem. And that's a game that actually <i>cares </i>about balancing stuff). It's ultimately a problem of playstiles. Of players (and ST) expecting different things of the game. It's a problem with the &quot;social contract&quot; of the game, the way people wants to play. That is, is a social problem.<br /> <br /> It's solved by talking. There's no other real way. That's how you will know what people wants, and people will know what you want.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Somethings I think you could try:<br /> <br /> Rather than sending the Technocracy to crush everyone (knowing that the PG it's the most likely to live trough it), let it be known that he's <i>&quot;the best gunslinger in the west&quot; . </i>This is bound to happen either by feats of the player (that's, I imagine, not hidding his power) or by his massive magical aura. People will want to go after him, either to duel, manipulate or even to learn from him. That can be a lot of fun, aknowledges that he's very powerful and &quot;on a different level&quot; (which ain't always good, but can be flattering if done in good fun).<br /> <br /> Have challenges of different natures (and levels) that the other players can enjoy. Think about what they're good at and engineer situations where those powers could come in handy. Maybe someone it's better at talking, maybe one it's better at getting intel about the enemies. Make situations that can't be solved by kicking the doors and being the strongest man arround. This works very well if the different players have different agendas and strengths.<br /> <br /> Fights aren't always symmetrical. Make figths against big groups of enemies that demand to split the party, since the PG can't be in more than one place at the same time (until he reaches Correspondence 4) the rest it's going to have their fun. If they're cooperative, having more (if weaker) people tossing stuff at a stronger enemy may be what wins the fight in the end, even for the PG point of view (not everyone has to be the MVP, right?).<br /> <br /> This doesn't work if all the players want to kick assess the same way, and will feel useless if one it's much more &quot;valuable&quot; in figths than the others. In that case, me thinks you will need to either tone him down (again) OR tone the others up giving them more &quot;optimal strategies&quot; (heck, your PG may even help you with that)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-04-2019, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T13:09:13-07:00","id":1339686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339337-rituals-and-their-usage?p=1339447#post1339447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You should. As with the &quot;too much magick aura&quot; it's mostly something that marks you as weird, altrough it can have more impactful and evident effects if it's very strong. As per M20 this is talked on Book of Secrets and the core<br /> <br /> This it's not something that can be solved with any amount of ruling (nor RAW nor Homemade). Much more &quot;balanced games&quot; can have this problem (I know D&amp;D players <i>have</i> this problem. And that's a game that actually <i>cares </i>about balancing stuff). It's ultimately a problem of playstiles. Of players (and ST) expecting different things of the game. It's a problem with the &quot;social contract&quot; of the game, the way people wants to play. That is, is a social problem.<br /> <br /> It's solved by talking. There's no other real way. That's how you will know what people wants, and people will know what you want.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this can't be emphasised enough.<br /> <br /> If that single player is creating a situation that is outside of the rest of the play experience and expectation then no in-game consequences or situation is going to really be comfortable or resolve it. A sit down, open conversation about &quot;just because you can, doesn't mean you must&quot; that is based upon respecting the game that you and the other players want to create is the best way to resolve it. The player's approach to this conversation will indicate whether they are prepared and able to respect boundaries that benefit the other participants in the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't really see much in-game response being a great deal of fun for everyone at the gaming table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/133-guinbang","name":"guinbang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T07:16:01-07:00","id":1340410,"title":"","content":"well, since they did trigger some Technocratic feelers at some point, they are bound to go after them. I have several ideas on how to handle the situation. <br /> While rituals are extremely OP and can cause issues, I can handle them, in a way. My main concern was that maybe there was something that I'm missing and that is why they are OP, not because of the system itself.<br /> <br /> I mean, so far, none of the rituals are exactly gamebreaking so it can be handled, as the team itself has some holes in the setup (lack of spirit sphere for one) so they depend on NPCs for those. And it's hard to be OP when you don't have a clue <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> on a similar/related note:<br /> if a player has taken Node/Sanctum/Cult backgrounds, how deep in shit should he get into before he starts losing those? I mean, they are paid with points so I'm a bit reluctant to take away those, but how do you handle that? Does the player need to really draw attention to himself to have those affected or? And if he loses that, how do you resolve him/her getting it back?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25677-danzaburo","name":"Danzaburo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T09:46:06-07:00","id":1340429,"title":"","content":"Welllll.<br /> <br /> Cults in particular are actually a high-maintenance background. The Mage has to take *care* of their followers. They have to talk to them. Perform acts that fit into the cult's belief. Keep the social bonds to them up. Be the Cult leader they want them to be, while steering the Cult towards how they want the cult to be. It demands good social skills.<br /> Cults are also where the Technocracy can put in the prybar, especially the NWO. The NWO can make the lives of Cultists bad through subtle ways; Spreading the word to their employers that they are in some cult. Subtly push the rumor mill among their friends and families. Let society do the rest. It *can* backfire by drawing in more cultists, but the NWO has a lot of experience in making the stuff seem bad.<br /> <br /> Sanctums? Well, a Sanctum first needs to be found. Then it depends on the type of sanctum. A rented home? Oh dear, the renter somehow got convinced to toss the Mage out. An owned home? Let's have the city take a close look at the building regulations. That don't work? Too bad it wasn't protected well. Those burglars sure did a number on it.<br /> Depending on how much that Sanctum is seen as a threat, that gas line explosion was a shame. A real shame.<br /> Sanctums out in rural nature and surroundings have an easier time staying hidden. So do Sanctums that quite frankly are simply not the Mage's home in the first place.<br /> The best way to protect your Sanctum is not to make your Mage-ey affiliation known to big enemies in the first place. We come full circle to Mages with lots of running effects being a beacon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Nodes on the other hand are always something that tends to lead to more drastic measures. There are times when rival Mages from *the same faction* try to get their hands on anothers. Nodes are Big Targets in the Ascension war. Most Mages make sure they are well hidden, protectied, and on a need-to-know basis unless they are actually fortified by a Chantry in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-09-2019, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T10:20:31-07:00","id":1340438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Danzaburo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339337-rituals-and-their-usage?p=1340410#post1340410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> on a similar/related note:<br /> if a player has taken Node/Sanctum/Cult backgrounds, how deep in shit should he get into before he starts losing those? I mean, they are paid with points so I'm a bit reluctant to take away those, but how do you handle that? Does the player need to really draw attention to himself to have those affected or? And if he loses that, how do you resolve him/her getting it back?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can understand the reluctance of taking away backgrounds, and it will always be a challenging point depending upon the nature of the players themselves. I don't think it's &quot;deep in shit&quot; question, so much as what investment is required to maintain them.<br /> <br /> I think that there are three important points to bear in mind:<br /> <br /> 1. The possibility of change is known to everyone at the start, along with the kinds of in game actions that may lead to change<br /> 2. The players' actions influence whether they go down or not as a natural consequence of their in game actions<br /> 3. They can go up as well as go down as natural consequences of those actions<br /> <br /> Natural consequence may take some explicit explanation: &quot;If you guys and gals use lots of vulgar magick you are going to attract Technocracy attention and they are known to do all of the things that Ambrosia mentions. This is targeting your characters through your background points rather than their health levels.&quot; (For instance)<br /> <br /> <br /> Part of establishing your answers to these three points is also asking yourself what kind of game you want to play. If you're after a game of Cultist Simulator, then Cults do need a lot of screen time to maintain. If you are more interested in Cults as being a mechanical way to get more dice for the Rituals, then it can be hand-waved away with no great loss or benefit to the character / player. The middle path, that the leadership of the Cult is important but not dominant, means that there are potentially story complications. For instance, perhaps they need to attend the cult centre every Sunday morning without fail, having spent time preparing a speech to deliver to their loyal people.<br /> <br /> Establishing up front that if they don't meet that commitment means the background would reduce with some fictional parallel to reflect that (e.g. the cult fractures and half of the cultists join up with a rival leader). But if they knock those speeches out of the park, funnel some incentives into a recruitment drive... Well then the Cult could expand as well.<br /> <br /> One missed meeting is neither here nor there - but that extended trip to find a mentor to learn the Spirit suddenly becomes a question of balancing that priority with the maintenance of the Cult.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> An alternative way to look at this, if you want the story but don't want to lose the mechanic is that the dots are temporarily lost for part of the story but the character has a really easy time getting them back. For instance, through attracting the wrong kinds of attention, the NWO raid the sanctum causing the character to flee. Fortunately, they already had a backup plan and over the course of the next session or two they quickly build the Sanctum back up without having to reinvest XP or other resources. This may only work once or possibly twice without stretching believability (&quot;Hey its nine Sanctum Sammy moving in next door... again!&quot; but provides a softer way to show backgrounds are fluid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/133-guinbang","name":"guinbang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T11:33:34-07:00","id":1340449,"title":"","content":"Wait, doesn't having a change with Life 3 generate pattern bleeding every day?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T22:41:24-07:00","id":1340554,"title":"","content":"Not if it is within the limits of your natural pattern - i.e. staying within human natural limits in stats, abilities, physiology and cosmetics. As soon as you go above them, or add/change anything to your body that is not a thing normal humans have, you get the pattern bleed. And then you can only stave it off by spending 1 quint per day, or get rid of it by stopping the effect or making things permanent, which means keeping the permadox or genetic flaws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T05:41:38-07:00","id":1340598,"title":"","content":"&quot;an organism that has been radically altered by Life magick (given new limbs or other characteristics that are not part of the creature\u2019s original Pattern) suffers Pattern bleeding: an inexorable Quintessence leak that inflicts one level of lethal damage per day. Unless the caster uses Prime magick to refill that Pattern with fresh energy, or alters that Pattern permanently, the damage continues until the subject dies.&quot;<br /> <br /> You're right. I swear i thought that any change that lasted more than 1 day dealed patter bleeding...<br /> <br /> How can s mage use Prime to refill the pattern and avoid bleeding? If I remember correctly, revised let you spend 1 quint to avoid it..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T10:12:57-07:00","id":1340638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339337-rituals-and-their-usage?p=1340598#post1340598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;an organism that has been radically altered by Life magick (given new limbs or other characteristics that are not part of the creature\u2019s original Pattern) suffers Pattern bleeding: an inexorable Quintessence leak that inflicts one level of lethal damage per day. Unless the caster uses Prime magick to refill that Pattern with fresh energy, or alters that Pattern permanently, the damage continues until the subject dies.&quot;<br /> <br /> You're right. I swear i thought that any change that lasted more than 1 day dealt patter bleeding...<br /> <br /> How can s mage use Prime to refill the pattern and avoid bleeding? If I remember correctly, revised let you spend 1 quint to avoid it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you utilize quintessence on a pattern you need Prime to be able to control it. Although you can freely use quintessence to lessen difficulty modifiers on rotes it's not the same as fueling a pattern since you actually need to understand the very concept of pattern that Prime gives off.<br /> Well if it's on your own body I think it should be okay to not use prime 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24274,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","user":"menos125","date":". 10-10-2019, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T13:28:25-07:00","id":1340673,"title":"","content":"The bleeding will depend of one's interpretation of &quot;radically&quot;. Is soaking lethal /agg radical? And getting 5 in all physical attributes? <br /> <br /> Also, whenever the mage suffer pattern bleeding he also suffer permadox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T15:18:36-07:00","id":1340689,"title":"","content":"I imagine the context of the stats matters to. Going from 4-5 Strength is probably ok. Going from 1-5 Strength is probably not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T16:56:45-07:00","id":1340701,"title":"","content":"All 5s is still not past human ability so even though we agree its unlikely it's still within limits. <br /> <br /> I dont remember if soaking lethal is consider to cause patern bleeding but if the conditions make the casting vulgar I would probably impose it. Soaking aggravated is always vulgar and definitely causes patern bleeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T07:46:24-07:00","id":1340776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339337-rituals-and-their-usage?p=1340429#post1340429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welllll.<br /> <br /> Cults in particular are actually a high-maintenance background. The Mage has to take *care* of their followers. They have to talk to them. Perform acts that fit into the cult's belief. Keep the social bonds to them up. Be the Cult leader they want them to be, while steering the Cult towards how they want the cult to be. It demands good social skills.<br /> Cults are also where the Technocracy can put in the prybar, especially the NWO. The NWO can make the lives of Cultists bad through subtle ways; Spreading the word to their employers that they are in some cult. Subtly push the rumor mill among their friends and families. Let society do the rest. It *can* backfire by drawing in more cultists, but the NWO has a lot of experience in making the stuff seem bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmm.. well, if (s)he has life magic, simply being a sort of a faith healer is enough in terms of taking care of the followers and keep their dedication up, at least from my point of view. I mean, we could go more into Cult management and all that, but I feel that would be dull for both me and the players <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I can see where you are going with Technocracy though. Especially if it becomes too wide-spread and shows up under their radar since people with serious illness get healed basically overnight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sanctums? Well, a Sanctum first needs to be found. Then it depends on the type of sanctum. A rented home? Oh dear, the renter somehow got convinced to toss the Mage out. An owned home? Let's have the city take a close look at the building regulations. That don't work? Too bad it wasn't protected well. Those burglars sure did a number on it.<br /> Depending on how much that Sanctum is seen as a threat, that gas line explosion was a shame. A real shame.<br /> Sanctums out in rural nature and surroundings have an easier time staying hidden. So do Sanctums that quite frankly are simply not the Mage's home in the first place.<br /> The best way to protect your Sanctum is not to make your Mage-ey affiliation known to big enemies in the first place. We come full circle to Mages with lots of running effects being a beacon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Nodes on the other hand are always something that tends to lead to more drastic measures. There are times when rival Mages from *the same faction* try to get their hands on anothers. Nodes are Big Targets in the Ascension war. Most Mages make sure they are well hidden, protectied, and on a need-to-know basis unless they are actually fortified by a Chantry in the first place. </div> </div> </div>well, I have no shortage of ideas on HOW to do it, it was always a problem on why and all that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I mean, if a PC has both Sanctum and Node at the same place, it would be really shitty of me to have it all gone without a good reason. Ergo, my initial question, how bad should the PC mess up before I can (as a ST) justify taking those? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guinbang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339337-rituals-and-their-usage?p=1340438#post1340438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can understand the reluctance of taking away backgrounds, and it will always be a challenging point depending upon the nature of the players themselves. I don't think it's &quot;deep in shit&quot; question, so much as what investment is required to maintain them.<br /> <br /> I think that there are three important points to bear in mind:<br /> <br /> 1. The possibility of change is known to everyone at the start, along with the kinds of in game actions that may lead to change<br /> 2. The players' actions influence whether they go down or not as a natural consequence of their in game actions<br /> 3. They can go up as well as go down as natural consequences of those actions<br /> <br /> Natural consequence may take some explicit explanation: &quot;If you guys and gals use lots of vulgar magick you are going to attract Technocracy attention and they are known to do all of the things that Ambrosia mentions. This is targeting your characters through your background points rather than their health levels.&quot; (For instance)<br /> <br /> <br /> Part of establishing your answers to these three points is also asking yourself what kind of game you want to play. If you're after a game of Cultist Simulator, then Cults do need a lot of screen time to maintain. If you are more interested in Cults as being a mechanical way to get more dice for the Rituals, then it can be hand-waved away with no great loss or benefit to the character / player. The middle path, that the leadership of the Cult is important but not dominant, means that there are potentially story complications. For instance, perhaps they need to attend the cult centre every Sunday morning without fail, having spent time preparing a speech to deliver to their loyal people.<br /> <br /> Establishing up front that if they don't meet that commitment means the background would reduce with some fictional parallel to reflect that (e.g. the cult fractures and half of the cultists join up with a rival leader). But if they knock those speeches out of the park, funnel some incentives into a recruitment drive... Well then the Cult could expand as well.<br /> <br /> One missed meeting is neither here nor there - but that extended trip to find a mentor to learn the Spirit suddenly becomes a question of balancing that priority with the maintenance of the Cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think they are all aware that their backgrounds can go sour at some point. Although, I'm not sure if they realise that is is relatively easy to lose them.<br /> As for Cult, I really do not want to go through Cult Simulator mode and would like to keep the Cult experience to a bare minimum. Although, I like the idea of a repeated presence being required as to keep the Cult up, so they can't just go missing for weeks and expect everything to be there still.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An alternative way to look at this, if you want the story but don't want to lose the mechanic is that the dots are temporarily lost for part of the story but the character has a really easy time getting them back. For instance, through attracting the wrong kinds of attention, the NWO raid the sanctum causing the character to flee. Fortunately, they already had a backup plan and over the course of the next session or two they quickly build the Sanctum back up without having to reinvest XP or other resources. This may only work once or possibly twice without stretching believability (&quot;Hey its nine Sanctum Sammy moving in next door... again!&quot; but provides a softer way to show backgrounds are fluid. </div> </div> </div>That is what I was thinking about, having it fluid. But, my main concern was grappling with the same thing you said in the end: how much is too much? and how easy should it be? I mean, are there any instructions on how a Sanctum is built? I don't recall seeing any... Of course, I can make it up as I go along, but apart from arranging it to your pattern etc., are there any spheres involved? any wards?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, rituals that confuse me are the Mind rituals. <br /> It seems that you can do pretty nasty stuff with only Mind one (Mind Shield, Multitasking, Mental trait improvement...) with the Multitasking one being the most vague. How do you see that one? How many actions/tasks can a character do with, say, 2 successes? <br /> I mean, based on the books and based on the 2nd edition source book (since it is there actually explained), it seems that character can do 3 simultaneous tasks. <br /> However, the borders/boundaries of those tasks are not defined. Yes, he is restricted by physical constraints (he can't fire and jack himself off with the same hand) but, for example, casting a spell whose focus is verbal and firing? casting a spell and dodging? doing a small ritual and keeping watch? fixing a car and programming a computer?<br /> lockpicking with one hand and firing a gun with the other?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25677-danzaburo","name":"Danzaburo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T15:02:00-07:00","id":1341010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339337-rituals-and-their-usage?p=1340689#post1340689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine the context of the stats matters to. Going from 4-5 Strength is probably ok. Going from 1-5 Strength is probably not.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, if the mage is going to make it last only one day he might as well just go full buffed and go beyond 5. That way he won't deal with pattern bleeding. Only with a permadox that will vanish at the end of the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T15:53:38-07:00","id":1341013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339337-rituals-and-their-usage?p=1341010#post1341010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, if the mage is going to make it last only one day he might as well just go full buffed and go beyond 5. That way he won't deal with pattern bleeding. Only with a permadox that will vanish at the end of the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya that's the best way to meta game it for sure. The only downside is how long the ritual to increase the Stats takes which is really determined by the caster's belief. If your Akashic or something similar where a hour of meditation let's you get in all your rolls it's pretty easy. If it's an Etherite using gene modification it might be a bit prolonged and therefore prohibitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T08:15:53-07:00","id":1341442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339337-rituals-and-their-usage?p=1340554#post1340554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not if it is within the limits of your natural pattern - i.e. staying within human natural limits in stats, abilities, physiology and cosmetics. As soon as you go above them, or add/change anything to your body that is not a thing normal humans have, you get the pattern bleed. And then you can only stave it off by spending 1 quint per day, or get rid of it by stopping the effect or making things permanent, which means keeping the permadox or genetic flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>The word original is important in the description I posted.<br /> Does it means that any change that was not part of the original pattern (any change at all, lol) deals pattern bleed?<br /> <br /> Also, it seems that in M20 permadox only applies when the effect is going to be permanent, is that correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T10:06:12-07:00","id":1341464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339337-rituals-and-their-usage?p=1341442#post1341442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it means that any change that was not part of the original pattern (any change at all, lol) deals pattern bleed?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because then it would say 'Any change causes pattern bleed'.<br /> As long as you stay a normal human, within human limits, human limbs, organs and whatever makes you not a freak of nature, there is a no bleed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T12:35:31-07:00","id":1341492,"title":"","content":"@Ambrosia-- It could be the editions I'm most familiar with, but I was pretty sure that pattern bleed was caused by raising attributes in general, and you get permadox for going outside those limits. Also, to my knowledge, complete transformation into other consensus-friendly creatures causes neither pattern bleed nor permadox, but carries the risk of you forgetting what you are supposed to be and not changing back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T13:18:35-07:00","id":1341499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339337-rituals-and-their-usage?p=1341464#post1341464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, because then it would say 'Any change causes pattern bleed'.<br /> As long as you stay a normal human, within human limits, human limbs, organs and whatever makes you not a freak of nature, there is a no bleed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically if it is coincidental, then there's no bleed?<br /> <br /> In rev any change resulted in bleed. You think this is different in M20? <br /> <br /> About permadox it seems pretty clea that in M20, it is only a result of permanent effects. You're right if you meant revised though @faradn<br /> <br /> So, it's :<br /> Simple temporary(more than 1 day) changes - nothing<br /> Radical temporary (more than 1 day)changes (attributes above 5, limbs, armor,etc.) - Pattern bleed<br /> Radical permanent changes - permadox","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T22:52:30-07:00","id":1341576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339337-rituals-and-their-usage?p=1341492#post1341492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Ambrosia-- It could be the editions I'm most familiar with, but I was pretty sure that pattern bleed was caused by raising attributes in general, and you get permadox for going outside those limits. Also, to my knowledge, complete transformation into other consensus-friendly creatures causes neither pattern bleed nor permadox, but carries the risk of you forgetting what you are supposed to be and not changing back.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's indeed messy with the different wordings between different editions.<br /> You get pattern bleeding (Called pattern leakage in 2nd ed, amusingly enough) even when shifting into other consensus-friendly beings - because the same rule applies, you've moved away from your original pattern.<br /> <br /> And regarding pattern bleeding and human range, I've just been just re-reading the various materials, and man is it a mess. As usual.<br /> <br /> 2nd Ed - Clearly states that any change that is non-cosmetic causes Pattern Bleed/Leakage. Also states that Pattern Bleeding damage can only be healed naturally. Also, using a steady supply of quintessence can stave off the pattern bleed. Makes no mention of permanent paradox.<br /> <br /> Revised - States that any change that is non-cosmetic causes Pattern Bleed. Does *not* mention that it can only be healed naturally, and makes no mention of the Quintessence. But *does* mention that *swapping* attributes (i.e. keeping the total amount of attribute dots the same) might not cause pattern bleed. Permadox hits as soon as you move beyond human limits.<br /> <br /> M20 - The corebook entry is rather unclear and the source of my confusion - Simply saying that &quot;characteristics not part of the original pattern&quot; cause Pattern Bleed that can only heal naturally. Can be seen as human range, can be seen as the Mage's very specific attribute makeup. But this one *does* mention the staving-off of Pattern Bleed with Quintessence again, wee!<br /> HDYDT goes into more detail and says that Pattern Bleeding is, as usual, only as long as the modifications are not permanent, but also mentions that Permadox and/or genetic flaws only hit *when* they become permanent and are outside human limits. It also mentions that those permanent changes should be bought as the Enhancements background to make things permanent.<br /> <br /> So there we go, it highly depends on which edition you choose. 2nd and Revised seem to be clear about raising (or lowering!) attributes in any way causes pattern bleed. Revised hints at simply rebalancing the total points might circumvent it. M20 is very vague in regards to what 'original pattern' means and it might be as per 2nd or Revised, or it could mean 'Outside human range'.<i> It Prrrrrrrrobably means the mage's specific original pattern.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-16-2019, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}